  GEOMETRY, stated up front (bug pattern 2): everything below is the SPHERICAL-EQUIVALENT phantom, M_ph(<r) = (nu-1) g_bar r^2/G.
  That is not an approximation to what halo fitters do -- it is EXACTLY what they do: a rotation-curve halo fit defines
  V_halo^2(r) = G M_halo(<r)/r with M_halo spherical, so both sides of every comparison here carry the same geometry.  It IS an
  approximation to the true QUMOND phantom of a flattened disc, which is itself flattened, and no PROJECTED quantity is claimed
  anywhere below for that reason.
  phantom computed and Burkert-fitted for 147 SPARC galaxies; 147 also have a Li+2020 Burkert fit
  Burkert fit quality, fractional rms in the halo rotation curve: MODEL phantom median 0.047 (90th 0.091); DATA halo at the same Upsilon median 0.076
